WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.860
- All right, so we've talked
to Molly about her shows

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.940
that are just crushing it.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.310
I can think of something
else that might bring

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:13.490
that same fervor, and it's a
little movie called, Scream.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.980
(audience cheers)

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.980
So there is a new Scream coming out

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.293
and what I can gather,

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.250
and talking to Courtney,

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:33.250
and a few of the alumni and
a few of the new cast members

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.830
is that they're taking an interesting

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.010
and different approach.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.493
Can you tell me anything?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.090
Without getting arrested in movie jail.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.980
- I can tell you that I love
playing the role of Dewey.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.903
It's such an iconic role, thank you.

00:00:48.903 --> 00:00:51.070
(audience cheers)

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.840
That Matt and Tyler were inspired by Wes

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.690
to become filmmakers.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.960
They're the two directors
that are part of a group

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.130
called Radio Silence that did the film.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.470
But they were inspired by Wes,

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.740
so they really wanted to make a tribute,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.293
like a real something
that he'd be proud of.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.670
And there's an incredible cast.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.283
I mean, I think people are
really going to be excited by it.

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:13.334
- I think-

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.720
- I can't say anything 'cause
I'm talking in circles.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.647
- I don't know you guys are-

00:01:17.647 --> 00:01:19.620
- It's like I'm falling fishing.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.220
- You guys are Angelinas,

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.160
do you all know about

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.964
the Hollywood Forever cemetery screenings?

00:01:24.964 --> 00:01:25.797
- [Audience] Yes.

00:01:25.797 --> 00:01:28.260
- Okay, these things are legendary.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:33.100
I mean, I'm talking five, 7,000
people show up on the night

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.820
to go to a cemetery and watch movies.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.830
And they did a slumber
party just a few weeks ago.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.900
I know because also
Billie Eilish texted me

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.890
and showed me that she
dressed up as Casey Becker.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:50.050
And I've recently made friends with her.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:50.930
I'm freaking out.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.290
- [David] Oh my God.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:55.410
- And it's like, you
have literally legends,

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.300
like Billie Eilish showing up for this.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.310
This movie has stood the test of time.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.670
It's capturing the hearts

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:04.400
of our generation, new generations.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.590
And a film like that
deserves not just a sequel,

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.740
but a re-invention and a
respect for the classic.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:14.600
(audience cheers)

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.597
I'm really excited about that.

00:02:16.597 --> 00:02:19.480
And it'll be great for you and I

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.612
to see that legacy alive and well.

00:02:22.612 --> 00:02:25.195
(upbeat music)

00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:28.980
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.852
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

